            "review_title": "Review at Pastel Cafe",
            "review_text": "Евгения Н\nProtvino, Russia1 contribution\n0\nI do not advise!\nMar 2024 • Couples\nWe dined here three times. The first time, everything was wonderful, the dishes corresponded to what was stated on the menu, and the wine was delicious. The second time we visited, we ordered a bottle of wine, white Chilean, but received some kind of barmoth))) although the owner assured that it was Chile. The third time we ordered a salad with mango and shrimp, but the salad turned out to be without mango 😂, they presented it to the waiter (the owner was not there), the cook squealed like a pig, proving that she had included mango. It was difficult to prove something, they asked to call the owner (he is Russian), but this request was ignored.\nConclusion: you can go there to eat marinated tuna with new potatoes, tuna steak is also not bad, and with your own wine))) My husband liked the borscht and dumplings (this is the main reason for visiting this establishment))) In general, it is better to choose another restaurant. Don't ruin your nerves and health!!!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nShow original\nWritten March 12, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
